---
layout: base.njk
title: Industries
description: Industry-specific technology for Transportation and Logistics, Financial Services, Healthcare, Retail and Consumer, and Manufacturing. Deep patterns, shared standards, one team.
permalink: /industries/
---

<section class="section pt-20 md:pt-28 pb-16 md:pb-24">
  <div class="wrapper grid-edit">
    <div class="col-span-12">
      <h1 class="font-display font-medium text-hero leading-[0.98] tracking-[-0.035em] text-balance reveal-mask">
        <span>Where we</span>
        <span class="block italic text-ink-secondary">work most.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-8 md:mt-10 text-lg md:text-xl max-w-2xl text-ink-secondary reveal reveal-delay-2 pretty">
        Five industries with deep pattern libraries. Each with a stack we know and the people who have shipped inside it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section border-t border-ink-primary">
  <div class="wrapper">
    {% set industries = [
      { url: "/industries/transportation-logistics/", title: "Transportation and Logistics", blurb: "Telematics, dispatch intelligence, route optimization, fleet cloud FinOps.", color: "var(--color-pixel-yellow)" },
      { url: "/industries/financial-services/",       title: "Financial Services",            blurb: "Risk, fraud, regulatory reporting, and core platform integrations. Audit evidence built in.", color: "var(--color-pixel-cyan)" },
      { url: "/industries/healthcare/",               title: "Healthcare",                    blurb: "EHR integrations, population health, claims, clinical AI with HIPAA operations.", color: "var(--color-pixel-purple)" },
      { url: "/industries/retail-consumer/",          title: "Retail and Consumer",           blurb: "Unified commerce, customer data platforms, demand forecasting, peak-ready ops.", color: "var(--color-pixel-orange)" },
      { url: "/industries/manufacturing/",            title: "Manufacturing",                 blurb: "OT and IT data together, production analytics, S/4 modernization, plant ops.", color: "var(--color-pixel-blue)" }
    ] %}
    <ul>
      {% for ind in industries %}
        <li class="reveal reveal-delay-{{ (loop.index0 % 4) + 1 }}">
          <a href="{{ ind.url }}" class="group flex items-start gap-5 md:gap-8 py-10 md:py-14 border-t border-ink-primary {% if loop.last %}border-b{% endif %} transition-colors duration-300 hover:bg-bg-subtle">
            <span class="meta pt-2 text-ink-secondary shrink-0">{{ '0' + loop.index | string if loop.index < 10 else loop.index }}</span>
            <div class="flex-1 min-w-0 flex flex-col lg:flex-row lg:items-start lg:gap-14">
              <h2 class="font-display font-medium text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-[2.5rem] leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.02em] lg:w-[44%] lg:shrink-0 min-w-0 flex items-center gap-3">
                <span class="shrink-0" style="display:inline-block;width:.75rem;height:.75rem;background: {{ ind.color }}"></span>
                {{ ind.title }}
              </h2>
              <p class="mt-3 lg:mt-0 lg:flex-1 min-w-0 text-ink-secondary pretty">{{ ind.blurb }}</p>
            </div>
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" class="mt-3 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-1" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 8h12m0 0L9 3m5 5l-5 5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="square"/></svg>
          </a>
        </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-statement">
  <div class="wrapper grid-edit">
    <div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-5">
      <span class="meta section-number reveal" style="--accent: var(--color-brand-blue); color: var(--color-ink-inverse-secondary)">Not on the list?</span>
      <h2 class="font-display font-medium text-4xl md:text-5xl leading-[0.98] tracking-[-0.025em] mt-6 balance reveal">
        We work beyond these five.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-7 md:pl-8">
      <p class="text-ink-inverse-secondary max-w-xl pretty reveal reveal-delay-1">
        These are the industries where we have the deepest pattern libraries. Engagements also run in energy and utilities, hospitality, public sector, and media. If your industry is not listed, start a conversation and we will tell you honestly where our depth sits.
      </p>
      <a href="/contact/" class="btn bg-transparent text-ink-inverse border-ink-inverse-secondary mt-8 hover:bg-ink-inverse hover:text-ink-primary hover:border-ink-inverse reveal reveal-delay-2">
        Start a conversation
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10m0 0L8 3m4 4l-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="square"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
